name o5-06-belt-1
timeout 900
time 1999-03-24T21:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O5, SORTIE 6 OF 10 - AIRFIELD DEFENCE: BATAJNICA, 24-26 MARCH 1999.
# THE MISSILE LAYER, ALONE. THIS FILE IS THE CONTROL OF o5-07-jammed.fbm.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o5-airfield-defence.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it IS the control, of o5-07.
#
# THE ARENA, and every coordinate in it is [SET]. Batajnica lies at ~44.93 N 20.26 E [T4, approximate -
# doc/campaigns/o5-airfield-defence.md says so and this campaign does not improve on it]. FlightBox flies
# it under `--elev const` on a 0 m datum (the real field is ~80 m) and with NO TERRAIN MASKING (gap C4),
# so the Fruska Gora, the Danube valley and every mask a Serbian battery used do not exist here. The
# field's runway heading (110 deg) and length (3 000 m) are [SET]; nothing in this campaign lands.
#   the field       44.93000 20.26000, with the fuel farm, a hangar row, one hardened shelter and the
#                   runway aim point around it
#   the point defence  P-18 node at 20.24000 (on the field), S-125 at 20.16000 (7.9 km W), 2K12 at
#                   20.19000/44.95500 (5.7 km W, 2.8 km N), ZSU-23-4 at 20.25200 (0.7 km W)
#   the package     ingresses due east along 44.93 N from 19.60000 (52.0 km out) at 5 000 m and 450 kt
# Scale at this latitude: 1 deg of longitude = 78 800 m, 1 deg of latitude = 111 132 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION, AND ITS DIRECTION. The package that attacked Batajnica was F-15C, F-117 and cruise
# missiles [T4]; FlightBox flies F-16s for all three, which is declared and not hidden. THE F-15C ROW
# EXISTS AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT USED, and the reason was MEASURED in this round rather than assumed:
# `modules/air/FBAirModule` composes NO FIRE CONTROL, so `FBState::FireControl` is never written and all
# three of FBPilot's weapon-employment gates stay shut. Measured: an `f15c` with four AIM-120 designates
# at t = 8.6 s at 18.64 nm, holds `eng_locked = 1` for 28 s from 18.6 down to 8.8 nm, and never posts a
# WeaponRelease. A catalogue row is ACCEPTED as a FLIGHT MODEL, not as a combatant.
# The defender is the MiG-29 the 127th "Knights" actually flew - so unlike O1 and O3 the substitution
# here is on the ATTACKER's side, and it makes the attacker WEAKER than history (no F-117, no cruise
# missile, no AIM-7/AMRAAM mix from a 160 km radar). A FlightBox Batajnica in which the field still
# loses says something WEAKER than 1999 did, not stronger.
#
# THE TWO LAYERS CANNOT BOTH BE LIVE, AND IT IS THIS CAMPAIGN'S STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURE - stated in every
# file because a reader who skips it will read every result backwards.
#   1. A FlightBox SAM site has NO IFF INTERROGATOR (`modules/ground/FBSiteModule`: "a battery has no
#      IFF interrogator in this tree") and an FBRadarContact carries no identity by construction, so a
#      battery engages the NEAREST FIRM TRACK in its envelope whoever it belongs to. An AIRFIELD is
#      exactly the geometry in which the friendly aircraft are the nearest track: O1 could lay its CAP
#      outside its own umbrella, O5 cannot, because the defenders live under it.
#   2. `missions/FBMissionRunner` ENDS THE WHOLE RUN at the first flight-monitor K.O. (`FirstFlightKo`),
#      and a mission-killed F-16 falls from 5 000 m in about 122 s. So an air engagement and a bomb run
#      in one file are not two measurements, they are one measurement and a truncation.
# The answer taken is the one a real airfield takes and the only one this format can express: the
# missiles are HELD while the fighters are up (`set emcon hold <offS> <onS>`, the briefed emission plan
# of round C26) and free when they are not. Sorties 01-05 therefore measure the FIGHTER layer with the
# belt briefed quiet; 06-07 measure the MISSILE layer with no fighter airborne; the chain 08-10 lets the
# campaign's own attrition decide which layer is left. THE CAMPAIGN NEVER MEASURES BOTH AT ONCE, and any
# claim that it did would be manufactured.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WITH NO FIGHTER AIRBORNE, WHAT DOES THE FIELD'S OWN POINT DEFENCE DO TO A
# STRIKE PACKAGE? This is the first sortie of O5 in which the ground fires at all, and it is the layer
# the campaign's title is about. Three strikers, three aim points, one netted belt whose emission plan
# has been removed: `set emcon hold` alone, dark until something it RECEIVES wakes it.
#
# THE DOCTRINE IS DECLARED AND NOT PREFERRED. Every fire unit is `emcon hold` (a passive receiver, never
# a timer) and `autonomy hold` (cut off from the node it waits); the node transmits `wcs free`.
# doc/air-defence-network.md section 5 carries `free` and `hold` as the two poles and refuses to rank
# them; this campaign flies one of them and says which.
#
# THE OBJECTIVES ARE THE POINT OF THIS FILE, and they are the vocabulary round C12 built for O5:
#   `objective protect unit <fuel farm>` on both SAM positions - the defender's success is that
#      something does NOT happen, and this is the only line in the format that says so. It is VIOLATED
#      the instant the fuel farm dies, and the run ends there; the TIME of that line is the measurement.
#   `objective no_fire` on the ZSU-23-4 - the field's inner gun under weapons hold. Its false positive is
#      named rather than hidden: the package runs in at 5 000 m and the Shilka's ceiling is 1 500 m, so
#      it could not have fired at the package even if it were free. What the line therefore measures is
#      the ALTITUDE DECISION, and it is why a package accepts SAM exposure to stay out of the flak.
#   `objective avoid zone umbrella` on every striker - the exposure, in seconds, of an ingress that has
#      no way round the S-125's 35 km envelope.
#
# WHY NO HARDENED TARGET IS AN AIM POINT. `attack-hardened.fbm` measures it: a Mk 82's fragment field
# finishes an unprotected installation out to ~45 m and a hardened one needs ~8 m. The shelter and the
# runway are in every O5 file and NOTHING IN THIS PACKAGE CAN KILL THEM - a Mk 84 CCRP delivery on this
# arena lands 38-51 m out, which finishes a soft installation and leaves a shelter standing. That, plus
# `C17` (a runway has no state and cannot be closed), is why "the shelters survived" is never reported as
# a defensive success in this campaign.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 7fc2aa31eca722b7): ONE STRIKER OF THREE DENIED, AND THEN THE FIELD.
# `net JOIN` x3 at t = 3.9, 12 `net CUE`, first firm track t = 39.0 s, SEVEN `site LAUNCH` - four V-601
# at 28.1 / 27.5 / 20.5 / 19.9 km and three 3M9 at 16.2 / 10.6 / 11.2 km, each after its own sourced
# reaction time (`trackToLaunchS` 30.8 / 33.4 / 30.9 / 33.5 for the S-125 and 26.9 for the 2K12). ALL
# SEVEN GO TO THE SAME AIRCRAFT - one engagement channel, and the log says so rather than the doctrine.
# `m6stra` is combat-ineffective at t = 139.3 by a 2.31 m arrival against a 10.0 m fuze, the third of
# four V-601 (6.87 / 6.09 / 2.31 / 2.20 m). The two survivors release; `m6sa3` dies at t = 195.0 and
# `m6ful` at t = 226.0, and `protect unit m6ful` is VIOLATED at t = 226.1 - that timestamp is the
# verdict. `zone_umbrella_s` = 188.2-188.5 s per striker and the terminal zone is first entered at
# t = 198.6 s.
# ONE HONEST ABSENCE: the run ends at the `protect` violation, so the flak's `no_fire` and the strikers'
# own objectives are never CONCLUDED and publish no `mission OBJECTIVE` line at all. Read that as
# unknown, not as zero (doc/missions/verdict.md Gaps says so).
#
# READING RULE: exit 1 is the expected shape - it is the `protect` objective being lost, i.e. the FIELD
# BEING HIT, and its timestamp is the verdict. Read in this order: `net JOIN` (the belt comes up),
# `net CUE` with its two staleness terms, `site STATE ... to=TRACK/ENGAGE`, `site LAUNCH` with
# `trackToLaunchS`, the DETONATION lines with missM against each round's own fuze (V-601 10.0 m,
# 3M9 8.0 m), then `sms RELEASE ... store=mk84` and which aim points died. exit 2 would be a defect.

zone umbrella 44.93000 20.16000 35000 100 18000   # the S-125's published envelope, as geometry
zone field    44.93000 20.26000  6000   0  6000   # the terminal box: first entry is the time-on-target

net batajnica
  control m6nod
  link radio 60000 mast 8
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member m6nod
  member m6sa3 autonomy hold
  member m6sa6 autonomy hold
  member m6flk autonomy hold

unit m6stra
  team friendly
  flight st6 1
  module f16
  spawn 44.93000 19.60000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 44.94000 20.24000 5000 450
  objective kill unit m6nod
  objective avoid zone umbrella

unit m6strb
  team friendly
  flight st6 2
  module f16
  spawn 44.94500 19.60000 5150 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 44.93000 20.16000 5150 450
  objective kill unit m6sa3
  objective avoid zone umbrella

unit m6strc
  team friendly
  flight st6 3
  module f16
  spawn 44.91500 19.60000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 44.93800 20.25000 5000 450
  objective kill unit m6ful
  objective avoid zone umbrella

unit m6nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 44.94000 20.24000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free

unit m6sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93000 20.16000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 4
  objective protect unit m6ful
  objective survive

unit m6sa6
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 44.95500 20.19000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 3
  objective protect unit m6ful
  objective survive

unit m6flk
  module zsu23
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93300 20.25200 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold
  objective no_fire
  objective survive

unit m6ful
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93800 20.25000 ground 0.0 0

unit m6hgr
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93200 20.23500 ground 0.0 0

unit m6has
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93500 20.27000 ground 0.0 0

unit m6rwy
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 44.92700 20.27500 ground 0.0 0
